caption: Mastery and Boundaries

The ten ordinary forms cost 60 CP total in this adaptation. Under the current Shadow Arts Mastery standard, those Jutsu alone do not satisfy the 100-CP tree-investment requirement; qualifying Water Breathing Tree Advantages or later appended Jutsu may supply the remaining investment. Dead Calm adds 2 CP and, because it requires Potence 5, cannot be authored until Shadow Doyen Mastery or learned until Shadow Arts Mastery. The example also demonstrates three important boundaries: several attacks produced by one Jutsu remain legal under the one-Jutsu-per-action rule; finite crowd attacks use Extra Targets rather than Area; and a deep prerequisite graph can create a Secret Master Technique before the tree reaches seventeen Jutsu.
